 Delete `EvmBlock`/`EvmTransaction`; then `Timestamp` newtype, `PrivacyTracking`
 enum, `EventSignatureRow` struct, and the `12`→const fix — one commit each. The
 CLI flag-enums and `SourceKey` are a good follow-on.
+
+## Unsmell follow-ups — `EventSignatureRow` struct change (2026-11-01)
+
+Smells found next to the `EventSignatureRow` change but outside its changed
+lines. Each is self-contained.
+
+- **Event lookup key travels as three loose values.** `(chain_id, address,
+  event_name)` is threaded through `resolve_event` / `resolve_event_topic`
+  (`src/signatures.rs`), `SignatureCache::get`/`put`, `SqliteSignatureCache`
+  (`src/bin/chainfold/signature_cache.rs`) and
+  `EventSignatureCache::{get,insert}_event_signature`. Introduce an
+  `EventKey { chain_id, address, event_name }` in `signatures` (source-agnostic
+  primitives) with a conversion to the `ChainId`/`Address` form in the cache
+  layer. That also removes the twice-written `ChainId::new(chain_id),
+  &Address::from(address)` in the adapter. Public trait change: decide whether
+  `signatures` stays primitive-only.
+- **Adapter error mapping written twice.** `src/bin/chainfold/signature_cache.rs`
+  `get`/`put` both do `.map_err(|e| SignatureError::Cache(e.to_string()))`.
+  Give it one name (a `From<CacheError> for SignatureError` in the lib, or a
+  local fn).
+- **`signature` and `topic0` can disagree.** `EventSignatureRow` and
+  `ResolvedEvent` store both, but `topic0` is always keccak256 of `signature`.
+  Options: an `EventSignature` type that computes its topic on construction,
+  or keep both and check on read. Spans `signatures` and the cache.
+- **`ResolvedEvent.topic0: [u8; 32]`.** `signatures` is source-agnostic, so the
+  bytes stay raw there; the conversion now lives in
+  `event_signature_cache.rs` `From` impls. Revisit if `signatures` ever takes
+  an EVM dependency.
+- **Unused `EventSignatureCache::open`.** `src/evm/cache/event_signature_cache.rs:39`
+  has no callers; `open_in_memory` is test-only. Delete `open`, or keep both if
+  the standalone-open pattern of `log_cache.rs`/`erc20_cache.rs` is deliberate
+  (then `path: &str` → `&Path` across all three).
+- **Docs in `event_signature_cache.rs` and the adapter.**
+  - Module doc (lines 1-8) mixes mechanism ("cheap handle over the shared
+    connection"), the row's fields read back, the caller's reason
+    ("zero-network", also stated in `cache.rs` and `signatures.rs`) and naming
+    history. Rewrite as the cache's place in the system.
+  - `EventSignatureCache` type doc ("Durable SQLite-backed event-signature
+    cache.") restates the name plus mechanism.
+  - `open` doc is imperative, repeats `CacheDb::open`'s effects and reads the
+    body back. `open_in_memory`'s "Useful for tests." is a caller's reason,
+    also at `cache.rs:115`.
+  - "`abi_json` is null for rows cached before the column existed" is stated
+    in `signatures.rs` (`ResolvedEvent::abi_json`) and `cache.rs` schema; keep
+    one owner.
+  - `src/bin/chainfold/signature_cache.rs:1` "Adapter: implements…" joins two
+    ideas with a colon.
+- **`erc20_cache.rs` repeats the hand-rolled optional row.**
+  `src/evm/cache/erc20_cache.rs:114-121,151-158` use `query_map` + `rows.next()`
+  + `match` with an inline `len() == 32` check. Use `query_row(..).optional()`
+  and `Topic::from_slice` / `B256::try_from`, as `get_event_signature` now does.
